 69   c  INST$Physics Division, Oak Ridge National Laboratory, P.O. Box 2008,   
 69  #c       Oak Ridge, Tennessee 37831-6354, USA                              
 69   c  ABST$Experimental data on ground- and excited-state properties for all 
 69  3c  known nuclei with mass number A=69 have been compiled and evaluated.   
 69  4c  States populated in radioactive decay, as well as in nuclear           
 69  5c  reactions, have been considered. For these nuclei, level and decay     
 69  6c  schemes, as well as tables of nuclear properties, are given in detail. 
 69  7c  This work supersedes the 2013 evaluation by C.D.Nesaraja (2014Ne01).   
 69   c  CUT$All literature available up to April 1, 2023 have been considered. 
 69  2c  The NSR database (2014Pr09) (www.nndc.bnl.gov/nsr/) is the primary     
 69  3c  source for the bibliography.                                           
 69   C  CIT$NDS 207, 1 (2026)                                                  
 69   c  ACKN$I would like to express my gratitude to Jun Chen (MSU) for his    
 69  2c  valuable advice on evaluation techniques and the use of the ENSDF      
 69  3c  codes he developed. I am also thankful to Augusto Macchiavelli (ORNL)  
 69  4c  for insightful discussions on nuclear configurations. The efforts of   
 69  5c  the XUNDL compilers greatly contributed to optimizing the evaluation   
 69  6c  process. In addition, I appreciate the careful and thorough reviews    
 69  7c  provided by the referee and the editorial reviewer.                    
 69   c  FUND$Research sponsored by the Oak Ridge National Laboratory, managed  
 69  xc  by UT-Battelle, LLC for the US Department of Energy under contract     
 69  xc  number DE-AC05-00OR22725.                                              

