 69CR c  Except for updates on all theoretical values from 2019Mo01,            
 69CR2c  there have been no changes in this dataset from the previous           
 69CR3c  evaluation (ENSDF as of 4 April 2023), that is available               
 69CR4c  online by Balraj Singh.                                                
 69CR c                                                                         
 69CR c  2013Ta14: identification of {+69}Cr by fragmentation of                
 69CR2c  {+82}Se beam at 139 MeV/nucleon from coupled-cyclotrons at NSCL        
 69CR3c  facility by Be and W targets placed at the object position of A1900    
 69CR4c  fragment separator which was combined with S800 analysis beam line to  
 69CR5c  form a two stage separator system. The transmitted fragments were      
 69CR6c  analyzed event-by-event in momentum and particle identification. The   
 69CR7c  nuclei of interest were stopped in eight Si PIN diodes which provided  
 69CR8c  measurement of energy loss, nuclear charge and total kinetic energy.   
 69CR9c  The time-of-flight of each particle that reached the detector stack    
 69CRAc  was measured using plastic scintillators, Si detectors, and            
 69CRBc  parallel-plate avalanche counters. The simultaneous measurement of |DE 
 69CRCc  signals, the magnetic rigidity, total kinetic energy and the           
 69CRDc  time-of-flight (tof) provided identification of the atomic number,     
 69CREc  charge state and mass number.                                          
