 69MN c  2015Be32: {+69}Mn was produced as fission fragment from the            
 69MN2c  {+9}Be({+238}U ,F) reaction. E({+238}U)=345 MeV/nucleon from           
 69MN3c  the Radioactive-Isotope Beam Factory (RIBF) facility at RIKEN          
 69MN4c  bombarded a Be target. The fragments were separated with the Big-RIPS  
 69MN5c  separator combined with the ZeroDegree Spectrometer. Measured E|g,     
 69MN6c  I|g, |b|g, |b(t), |b|g(t) using the 5 silicon detectors of the         
 69MN7c  WAS3ABI array which was surrounded by the EURICA spectrometer          
 69MN8c  consisting of 12 HPGe EUROBALL cluster detectors and 18 small volume   
 69MN9c  LaBr{-3}(Ce) scintillators. 4300 {+69}Mn ions were implanted into Si   
 69MNac  detectors. Comparison to FRDM+QRPA model, KTUY+GT2 model and shell     
 69MNbc  model calculations.                                                    
 69MN c  2012Ga06: Summary and compilation of the discovery of the Mn isotopes. 
 69MN c  2011Da08,2002MaZN (thesis): Produced by projectile fragmentation of    
 69MN2c  {+86}Kr beam on 50 mg/cm{+2} thick Ta at 57.8 MeV/nucleon. Separated   
 69MN3c  by LISE2000 spectrometer at GANIL. Detector system included a          
 69MN4c  three-element Si-detector telescope containing a double-sided          
 69MN5c  silicon-strip detector (DSSSD) backed by a Si(Li) detector and         
 69MN6c  surrounded by four clover type EXOGAM Ge detectors. Product            
 69MN7c  identified by mass, atomic number, charge, energy loss and time of     
 69MN8c  flight. Measured isotopic T{-1/2} from timing correlation between      
 69MN9c  implanted ions and |b decay events. Fitting procedure included five    
 69MNac  parameters: |b-detection efficiency, background rate, mother, daughter 
 69MNbc  and granddaughter half-lives.                                          
 69MN c  1999Ha05: Produced by 1 GeV proton-induced spallation of U in a thick  
 69MN2c  UC{-2} target at the ISOLDE facility at CERN. Identification and       
 69MN3c  T{-1/2} measurements by chemically selective laser ionization and      
 69MN4c  |b{+-} delayed n counting with the Mainz 4|p{+3} He neutron detector.  
 69MN c  1997Be70: Produced by projectile fission of {+238}U on {+9}Be target   
 69MN2c  at 750 MeV/nucleon. Fission fragments separated with the FRS separator 
 69MN3c  at GSI and identified by combination of |DE-B|r-tof, and trajectory.   
 69MN4c  A total of 5 counts were assigned to {+69}Mn corresponding to cross    
 69MN5c  section of 0.4 nanobarns.                                              
