 69FE c  2015Li33: {+69}Fe produced by projectile fragmentation of {+86}Kr beam 
 69FE2c  on {+9}Be target at 140 MeV/nucleon beam using the Coupled Cyclotron   
 69FE3c  facility at the NSCL-MSU facility. The fragmentation products were     
 69FE4c  separated using the A1900 fragment separator. They were then           
 69FE5c  identified and delivered to the Beta Counting System surrounded by     
 69FE6c  the Segmented Germanium Array (SeGA) where the |b and |g radiation     
 69FE7c  were detected. Ten |g rays (250, 291, 446, 648, 663, 680, 880, 1105,   
 69FE8c  1582 and 1886 keV) as listed in Figure 2b of 2015Li33 from the         
 69FE9c  decay of {+69}Fe to {+69}Co were observed.                             
 69FEac  Measured half-life by time distribution of |b particles                
 69FEbc  detected in correlation with implanted {+69}Fe ions and gammas.        
 69FE c  2013Ma87: {+69}Fe produced by projectile fragmentation of {+86}Kr beam 
 69FE2c  on {+9}Be target at 140 MeV/nucleon beam using the Coupled Cyclotron   
 69FE3c  facility at the NSCL-MSU facility. The fragmentation products were     
 69FE4c  separated using the A1900 fragment separator and implanted on a DSSD   
 69FE5c  located within the NSCL |b-counting system. Identification was done    
 69FE6c  by tof and energy loss method. Detected |b and |g radiation by NSCL    
 69FE7c  beta counting system. Measured half-life by time distribution of       
 69FE8c  |b particles detected in correlation with implanted {+69}Fe ions.      
 69FE9c  The |b|g coincidence event in correlation with {+69}Fe implants        
 69FEac  were also detected, but the statistics were very low.                  
 69FEbc  Comparison were made with calculations using FRDM+QRPA and Df3a++CQRPA.
 69FE c  2011Da08,2002MaZN (thesis):{+69}Fe produced by projectile              
 69FE2c  fragmentation of {+86}Kr beam on 50 mg/cm{+2} thick Ta at              
 69FE3c  57.8 MeV/nucleon. Separated by LISE2000 spectrometer at GANIL.         
 69FE4c  Detector system included a three-element Si-detector telescope         
 69FE5c  containing a double-sided silicon-strip detector (DSSD) backed by a    
 69FE6c  Si(Li) detector and surrounded by four clover type EXOGAM Ge           
 69FE7c  detectors. Product identified by mass, atomic number, charge, energy   
 69FE8c  loss and time of flight. Measured isotopic T{-1/2} from timing         
