 69CO c  Includes Ta({+86}Kr,X) and {+58}Ni({+86}Kr,X)                          
 69CO c  2017Sp03: {+69}Co ions were produced by projectile fragmentation of    
 69CO2c  {+86}Kr beam on {+9}Be target at 140 MeV/nucleon beam using the        
 69CO3c  Coupled Cyclotron facility at the NSCL-MSU facility. The fragmentation 
 69CO4c  products were separated using the A1900 fragment separator and         
 69CO5c  identified based on energy-loss and time-of-flight. The beam ions were 
 69CO6c  implanted into a double-sided silicon strip detector (DSSD) for |b     
 69CO7c  detection surrounded by the Summing NaI detector (SuN) of eight        
 69CO8c  segments for detecting emitted |g rays. Measured implant-|b(t),        
 69CO9c  |g rays. Deduced T{-1/2}.                                              
 69CO c  2015Li33: {+69}Co ions were produced by projectile fragmentation of    
 69CO2c  {+86}Kr beam on {+9}Be target at 140 MeV/nucleon beam using the        
 69CO3c  Coupled Cyclotron facility at the NSCL-MSU facility. The fragmentation 
 69CO4c  products were separated using the A1900 fragment separator. They were  
 69CO5c  then identified and delivered to the Beta Counting System surrounded   
 69CO6c  by the Segmented Germanium Array (SeGA) where the |b and |g radiation  
 69CO7c  were detected. {+69}Co was also populated in the decay of {+69}Fe      
 69CO8c  (see the {+69}Fe decay dataset). Five |g rays (594.2 {I602}.4, 1128.5, 
 69CO9c  1196.3 and 1319 keV) from the decay of {+69}Co to {+69}Ni were         
 69COac  observed.                                                              
 69CObc  Measured half-life by time distribution of |b particles                
 69CObc  detected in correlation with implanted {+69}Co ions and gammas.        
 69CO c  2011Da08,2002MaZN (thesis): {+69}Co ions produced by projectile        
 69CO2c  fragmentation of {+86}Kr beam on 50 mg/cm{+2} thick Ta at 57.8         
 69CO3c  MeV/nucleon. Separated by LISE2000 spectrometer at GANIL. Detector     
 69CO4c  system included a three-element Si-detector telescope containing a     
 69CO5c  double-sided silicon-strip detector (DSSD) backed by a Si(Li) detector 
 69CO6c  and surrounded by four clover type EXOGAM Ge detectors. Product        
 69CO7c  identified by mass, atomic number, charge, energy loss and time of     
 69CO8c  flight. Measured isotopic T{-1/2} from timing correlation between      
 69CO9c  implanted ions and |b decay events. Fitting procedure included five    
 69COac  parameters: |b-detection efficiency, background rate, mother, daughter 
 69CObc  and granddaughter half-lives.                                          
 69CO c  2005NiZZ,2004NiZY: Produced by fragmentation of {+73}Kr beam at        
 69CO2c  63 MeV/nucleon on a {+86}Kr{+32+} at RIKEN. Separated by RIPS          
 69CO3c  spectrometer and identified with silicon and tof detectors.            
 69CO4c  Preliminary results of T{-1/2} determined from correlations between    
 69CO5c  implanted nuclei and beta decay.                                       
 69CO c  1999So20 (also 1999Le67): {+69}Co ions produced by fragmentation of    
 69CO2c  {+86}Kr beam on {+58}Ni target at 60.4 MeV/nucleon. Nuclei separated by
 69CO3c  LISE3 achromatic spectrometer at GANIL, and identified by four         
 69CO4c  consecutive silicon detectors. Measured isotopic T{-1/2} from timing   
 69CO5c  of |b decay.                                                           
 69CO c  1992We04: {+69}Co ions produced by fragmentation of a 500 MeV/nucleon  
 69CO2c  {+86}Kr beam on a Be target. Isotope identification by the fragment    
 69CO3c  separator FRS at GSI in combination with tof and energy-loss           
 69CO4c  measurements. A total of 190 counts were assigned to {+69}Co           
 69CO5c  corresponding to cross section of 0.49 microbarns with an uncertainty  
 69CO6c  of 50%.                                                                
 69CO c  1985Gu14: {+69}Co ions produced by fragmentation of {+86}Kr beam on    
 69CO2c  thick targets of Ti and Ta at 33 MeV. Separated by LISE triple focusing
 69CO3c  analyzer at GANIL. Identified through tof and |DE-E measurements. Mass 
 69CO4c  histograms of the production of neutron-rich isotopes of Co displayed  
 69CO5c  shows a peak corresponding to {+69}Co.                                 
