 69NI2c  Cyclotron Lab (MSU) by bombarding {+86}Kr beam at 140 MeV/nucleon on   
 69NI3c  a {+9}Be target. Reaction products were separated by the A1900         
 69NI4c  fragment separator and identified with a plastic scintillator detector 
 69NI5c  and 2 silicon PIN detectors. The selected isotopes were then implanted 
 69NI6c  in a 1 mm thickness DSSD located at the center of the SuN detector (16 
 69NI7c  in. by 16 in. NaI(Tl) scintillating detector). Signals from all        
 69NI8c  segments of SuN were summed together into a total absorption spectrum. 
 69NI9c  Measured total absorption spectrum. Deduced beta-decay branching       
 69NIac  ratios, parent half-life. The |b feeding intensities were              
 69NIbc  compared to shell model and QRPA calculations.                         
 69NI c                                                                         
 69NI cB IB$From fit to measured total absorption spectrum,                     
 69NI2cB the sum-of-segments spectrum, and the multiplicity spectrum            
 69NI2cB in 2019Ly02. Beta intensities were provided by first author,           
 69NI3cB S. Lyons, of 2019Ly02 via email communication to XUNDL compiler,       
 69NI4cB J. Chen (NSCL, MSU) on 17 October 2019. For pseudo-levels,             
 69NI2cB quoted branching ratios are for an energy band around quoted level     
 69NI3cB energies, with the band equivalent to the energy resolution of SuN     
 69NI4cB (2019Ly02). For those approximate values, their original uncertainties 
 69NI5cB from the author are much greater than the values themselves.           
 69NI cB LOGFT$Should be considered as approximate when I{|b} is approximate.   
 69NI cG RI$From |g-ray spectrum recorded within 1 s of arrival of directly     
 69NI2cG produced {+69}Co ion in 2015Li33. Corresponding values obtained from   
 69NI3cG {+69}Fe -> {+69}Co -> {+69}Ni decay chain (2015Li33) are given         
 69NI4cG in comments. 1999Mu17 intensities which have been converted to         
 69NI6cG absolute intensities by 2015Li33 are also given in the comments.       
 69NI7cG Values from 1999Mu17 and 2015Li33 are in disagreement, based on which  
 69NI8cG the existence of an isomeric state in {+69}Co and that the source      
 69NI9cG produced by 1999Mu17 contained both the activities (2015Li33)          
 69NI cG E(X)$The |g ray observed in the spectrum using the source from {+69}Fe 
 69NI2cG decay, but barely, if at all, in the spectrum obtained from            
 69NI3cG directly produced {+69}Co (2015Li33).                                  
 69NI cG E(Y)$Larger intensity observed in source from {+69}Fe decay suggests   
 69NI2cG that this |g ray depopulates a low-spin level in {+69}Ni (2015Li33)    
 69NI cG E(Z)$From 1999Mu17 not observed by 2015Li33                            
