 69NI c  2016Re20 (also includes 2018ReZY): E=74 MeV/nucleon (mid-target)       
 69NI2c  {+70}Ni secondary beam was produced by fragmentation of a              
 69NI3c  140 MeV/nucleon {+82}Se primary beam from the Coupled Cyclotron        
 69NI4c  Facility (CCF) at NSCL, on a 423 mg/cm{+2} {+9}Be production target.   
 69NI5c  Fragments were selected and purified with the A1900 separator          
 69NI6c  and impinged on a 281 mg/cm{+2} {+9}Be reaction target.                
 69NI7c  Reaction residues were detected and identified on an event-by-event    
 69NI8c  basis using the time-of-flight and energy-loss information with the    
 69NI9c  beamline timing detectors and the S800 spectrograph focal-plane        
 69NIac  detector system. Prompt |g rays were detected with the Gamma-Ray       
 69NIbc  Energy Tracking In-beam Nuclear Array (GRETINA) surrounding the        
 69NIcc  reaction target; delayed |g rays were detected with a CsI(Na) detector 
 69NIdc  array at the S800 focal plane. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin.           
 69NIec  Deduced levels, J, |p, knock-out cross sections. Comparisons with      
 69NIfc  shell-model calculations. |s=168 mb {I13} (2018ReZY)                   
