 69CU    70ZN(D,3HE)                   2016MO21,1978ZE04         26NDS    202601
 69CU  H TYP=FUL$AUT=C.D. NESARAJA$CIT=NDS 207, 1 (2026)$CUT=1-Apr-2023$        
 69CU c  2016Mo21,2014Mo08: A 200 nA deuteron beam produced by the              
 69CU2c  duoplasmatron ion source at the Alto facility in Orsay, France was     
 69CU3c  accelerated by the 15 MV tandem to an energy of 27 MeV. The beam       
 69CU4c  was transported to the enriched {+70}Zn target which was located       
 69CU5c  at the object focal point of the Enge spit-pole magnetic spectrometer. 
 69CU6c  The target was 18.7 {I9} |mg/cm{+2} thick and backed by carbon.        
 69CU7c  The angular distribution (d|s/d|W) measurements were performed at      
 69CU8c  spectrometer angles of 6|', 9|', 12|', 15|', 18|', 21|', and 24|'.     
 69CU9c  The elastic scattering measurement was also performed at these angles  
 69CUac  and at 30|' and 40|'.                                                  
 69CUbc  The light charged particles were measured with the focal-plane         
 69CUcc  detection system consisting of a 50 cm long position-sensitive         
 69CUdc  proportional counter for position of the particle. A proportional gas  
 69CUec  counter filled with isobutane was used to measure |DE, while a plastic 
 69CUfc  scintillator was used to measure the residual E{-particle} that was    
 69CUgc  located behind the position detector. A Faraday cup at zero degree     
 69CUhc  was used to measure the incident deuteron intensity. The position of   
 69CUic  the focal-plane detection system was adjusted for the kinematic        
 69CUjc  displacement and to maximize the resolution. The average resolution    
 69CUkc  for the excited states is |s=18 keV {I2}. Deduced (d|s/d|W) and        
 69CUlc  excitation energy.                                                     
 69CUmc  A distorted-wave Born approximation (DWBA), DWUCK-4                    
 69CUnc  code was used to analyze the angular distributions and obtain the      
 69CUoc  spectroscopic factors. Both zero-range (Zr) and finite-range (Fr) DWBA 
 69CUpc  (DWUCK-4) calculations were performed at bound state properties r{-0}  
 69CUqc  and a{-0} as given in the dataset below. Shell model calculations were 
 69CUqc  were done to reproduce the 3/2- and 5/2- states and predict            
 69CUrc  the |pf{-7/2} strength                                                 
 69CU c  1978Ze04: Deuteron beam with E=23.3 MeV bombarded thick Zn targets     
 69CU2c  at the Argonne National Laboratory 60 inch cyclotron.                  
 69CU2c  |DE-E surface barrier| detector telescope was used to measure |s(|q) at
 69CU2c  |q= 12|'-30|' with resolution (FWHM)<50 keV.                           
 69CU3c  DWBA code JULIE used for analysis of data.                             
 69CU cL E$From 2016Mo21 and 1978Ze04, except as noted. Uncertainties were      
 69CU2cL not provided by either authors.                                        
