 69CU cL T$From the time difference between the implantation and correlated     
 69CU2cL |g-transitions in 2016Ku11. All the observed |g-ray transitions below  
 69CU3cL the isomer were summed to produce the decay curve. The quoted          
 69CU4cL uncertainty is statistical only.                                       
 69CU cL G$From TDPAD method in 2016Ku11. Experimental R(t) function was        
 69CU2cL fitted by the theoretical curve and |h{+2}-minimization was applied.   
 69CU3cL The uncertainty quoted includes the statistical uncertainty {I8} and   
 69CU4cL the systematic uncertainty {I5} due to the variation of the magnetic   
 69CU5cL field at the target position. The authors of 2016Ku11 stated that the  
 69CU6cL sign of the g-factor was determined from the sign dependence of the    
 69CU7cL nuclear spin alignment as a function of the momentum distribution and  
 69CU8cL the E2 character of 189.7|g. The + sign is also in agreement with the  
 69CU9cL Shell Model calculations. Note that the g-factor of this state         
 69CUacL was measured using the same technique in the projectile fragmentation  
 69CUbcL experiment, {+9}Be({+76}Ge,Xg) in 2002Ge16 .                           
 69CU cL $Shell model calculations give g{+free}=+0.261 and g{+eff}=+0.226      
 69CU2cL using JUN45 interaction and g{+free}=+0.274 and g{+eff}=+0.236 using   
 69CU3cL jj44b interaction. The wave function of the state is dominated by      
 69CU4cL |pp{+1}{-3/2}~#|np{+1}{-1/2}g{+1}{-9/2} and                            
 69CU5cL |pp{+1}{-3/2}~#|nf{+4}{-5/2}p{+1}{-1/2}g{+3}{-9/2}.                    
