 69CU c  Includes {+197}Au({+70}Zn,X|g)                                         
 69CU c  2017CaZP: Two experiments were conducted at Argonne National           
 69CU2c  Laboratory                                                             
 69CU c  {+70}Zn({+48}Ca,X|g): {+69}Cu was populated via proton transfer        
 69CU2c  with the {+48}Ca beam at E=170 MeV impinging a {+70}Zn target.         
 69CU3c  The experimental setup consisted of the GRETINA spectrometer and the   
 69CU4c  CHICO2 charged particle detector. |E|g, I|g, |g|g coin and             
 69CU5c  |g|g|g coincidence were measured. Experimental results were compared   
 69CU6c  to Monte Carlo simulations. Angular distributions A{-2} and A{-4} were 
 69CU7c  determined and mulitpolarities deduced.                                
 69CU c  {+197}Au({+70}Zn,X|g): In the deep inelastic reaction, {+70}Zn beam at 
 69CU2c  E=430 MeV impinged a {+197}Au target. The experimental setup consisted 
 69CU3c  of the GAMMASPHERE multidetector array. |E|g, I|g, |g|g coin and       
 69CU4c  |g|g|g coincidence were measured.                                      
 69CU cG E$From Fig. 3.15 in 2017CaZP. No uncertainties were provided           
 69CU cG M$From A{-2} and A{-4} values taken from Tabella 3.1 in 2017CaZP       
