 69CU    70ZN(238U,XG)                 2012Di03                  26NDS    202601
 69CU  H TYP=FUL$AUT=C.D. NESARAJA$CIT=NDS 207, 1 (2026)$CUT=1-Apr-2023$        
 69CU c  2012Di03: Multinucleon transfer reaction in inverse kinematics.        
 69CU2c  E({+238}U)=6.33 MeV/nucleon bombarded a 1.3 mg/cm{+2} thick target.    
 69CU3c  The target-like reaction products were detected and identified in      
 69CU4c  the VAMOS spectrometer at GANIL facility. Atomic number of fragments   
 69CU5c  determined by energy loss information in several ionization chambers   
 69CU6c  and Si detectors. Mass was determined from the total kinetic energy    
 69CU7c  and the time-of-flight information. Prompt |g rays were measured       
 69CU8c  using 11 Clover Ge detectors from the EXOGAM array in coincidence with 
 69CU9c  recoils identified in VAMOS. Delayed |g rays were detected at the      
 69CUac  VAMOS focal plane by four high-purity Ge detectors.                    
 69CUbc  Measurement of half-life from |g(t) of 13/2+ isomer. Six delayed |g    
 69CUcc  rays emitted by this isomer are shown by blue diamonds in figure 1     
 69CUdc  of 2012Di03.                                                           
 69CU cG E$Six delayed |g rays emitted by this isomer are shown by blue diamonds
 69CU2cG in Figure 1 of 2012Di03. The gamma energies rounded to the nearest keV 
 69CU3cG given in this dataset by the evaluator are from the Adopted Gammas.    
 69CU4cG The origin of one |g ray near 190 keV is not clear.                    
