 69CU c  Includes {+198}Pt({+76}Ge,X|g), Ni({+86}Kr,X|g),                       
 69CU2c  {+208}Pb,{+130}Te({+64}Ni,X|g) and {+208}Pb({+58}Ni,X|g)               
 69CU c  2000Is01: Deep inelastic collisions with {+70}Zn                       
 69CU2c  beam at 566 MeV produced at the JAERI tandem booster facility          
 69CU3c  on a {+198}Pt target. Measured E|g, |g|g, I|g, fragment-|g coin and    
 69CU4c  deduced T{-1/2} of isomeric states using improved isomer scope         
 69CU5c  instrument consisting of Si and Ge detectors and |g-ray absorbers.     
 69CU6c  Anisotropies |g(|q) of fragment-|g rays measured by Ge detectors       
 69CU7c  placed in plane (|q=90|') and out of plane (|q=0|').                   
 69CU c  1998Gr14: Ni({+86}Kr,X|g). E({+86}Kr)=60.3 MeV/nucleon on natural Ni   
 69CU2c  target using Alpha and LISE3 spectrometers at GANIL. Measured E|g,     
 69CU3c  |g|g, |g(t) fragment-|g coincidence with Si planar and HPGe detectors. 
 69CU5c  Two isomeric states at E=321 keV and 2701 keV observed.                
 69CU6c  Deduced T{-1/2} of isomer.                                             
 69CU c  1999BrZS (Supersedes 1998BrZU): {+69}Cu produced by deep inelastic     
 69CU2c  collision of 350 MeV {+64}Ni and 345 MeV {+58}Ni on {+208}Pb target,   
 69CU3c  and 275 MeV {+64}Ni on {+130}Te target. Measured E|g, projectile-|g|g  
 69CU4c  coincidence and T{-1/2}                                                
 69CU c  2001Is02,1997Is13: Deep inelastic collisions with {+76}Ge              
 69CU2c  beam at E=635 MeV produced at the JAERI tandem booster facility        
 69CU3c  on a {+198}Pt target at |q{-grazing}= 35|'. Measured                   
 69CU4c  E|g, |g|g, fragment-|g coin and deduced T{-1/2} of isomeric states     
 69CU5c  using isomer scope instrument consisting of Si and Ge detectors        
 69CU6c  and |g-ray absorbers.                                                  
