 69CU c  No changes from XUNDL compiled dataset by                              
 69CU2c  J. Chen (NSCL, MSU), March 4, 2015.                                    
 69CU c  2015Sa09: Neutron-rich Cu isotopes were populated via multinucleon     
 69CU2c  transfer reactions using a E=577 MeV {+76}Ge beam from the Tandem-XTU  
 69CU3c  and the ALPI superconducting LINAC accelerators at Laboratori Nazionali
 69CU4c  di Legnaro (LNL), bombarding a thin, metallic {+238}U target of 1.5    
 69CU5c  mg/cm{+2} thickness evaporated onto a {+181}Ta backing of 1.4 mg/cm{+2}
 69CU6c  thickness. Reaction products were separated according to the measured  
 69CU7c  |DE-E matrix by the PRISMA magnetic spectrometer. |g rays were detected
 69CU8c  by the AGATA Demonstrator array of four triple clusters, each          
 69CU9c  consisting of three 36-fold segmented HPGe detector. Measured E|g, I|g,
 69CUac  particle-|g(t). Deduced lifetime of 1711 level using the differential  
 69CUbc  recoil-distance Doppler-shift method (RDDS), transition probabilities. 
 69CUcc  Compared with shell-model calculations.                                
