 69ZN    68ZN(D,P),(POL D,P)           1967VO05,1975IS04,1981BI0626NDS    202601
 69ZN  H TYP=FUL$AUT=C.D. NESARAJA$CIT=NDS 207, 1 (2026)$CUT=1-Apr-2023$        
 69ZN c  1981Bi06: E=10 MeV polarized deuteron beam from the University         
 69ZN2c  of Wisconsin Lamb-shift polarized ion source and tandem accelerator    
 69ZN3c  was incident on a 1.1 mg/cm{+2} Zn target. The reaction                
 69ZN4c  products were detected with |DE-E telescopes with FWHM=60 keV          
 69ZN5c  Measured |s(|q) with |q |? 15|'-80|' and vector                        
 69ZN6c  analyzing powers. DWBA analysis (DWUCK) including non-locality and     
 69ZN7c  finite range corrections were made.                                    
 69ZN c  1975Is04: E=7.5 MeV deuterons from the MIT-ONR Van de Graaff           
 69ZN2c  accelerator was incident on enriched {+68}Zn target. Measured |s(|q)   
 69ZN3c  and DWBA analysis was performed. Deduced levels, J|p and angular       
 69ZN4c  momentum transfer                                                      
 69ZN c  1967Vo05: E=10.0 MeV deuterons from the Argonne Tandem Van de Graaff   
 69ZN2c  bombarded and enriched {+68}Zn target. Measured                        
 69ZN3c  |s(|q) at |q=5|'-40|' using a magnetic spectrograph with               
 69ZN4c  FWHM=10-15 keV and at |q=25|'-165|' using surface barrier detectors    
 69ZN5c  with FWHM|? 50 keV. Statistical error in cross sections                
 69ZN6c  quoted to 30 % (see erratum in 1967Vo05). DWBA (Macefield) analysis    
 69ZN7c  was performed.                                                         
 69ZN c  1969Za04: Deuteron beam from the electrostatic generator at the        
 69ZN2c  Physics Division at the Ukrainian Academy of Sciences bombarded a      
 69ZN3c  {+68}Zn target. Protons were detected using four silicon               
 69ZN4c  detectors (FWHM=75-80 keV) with |q between 20|'-160|'. Measured        
 69ZN5c  |s(|q). Distorted wave method calculations were performed and          
 69ZN6c  compared with experimental angular distribution.                       
 69ZN c  1963Li06: E=15 MeV deuterons from the University of Pittsburgh         
 69ZN2c  cyclotron was incident on enriched {+68}Zn target. Reaction            
 69ZN3c  products were analyzed by magnetic spectrograph and detected by        
 69ZN4c  photographic plates with |q=9|'-59|' with resolution|? 90 keV.         
 69ZN5c  Measured |s(|q). DWBA analysis was performed and compared to the       
 69ZN6c  experimental results.                                                  
