 69ZN c  2015Ce03: {+69}Zn was produced using deep-inelastic reaction in        
 69ZN2c  inverse kinematics with a {+238}U beam at 6.76 MeV/nucleon impinging   
 69ZN3c  on a {+70}Zn target that was deposited on a thick Mg backing.          
 69ZN4c  {+69}Zn ions were identified event-by-event using a VAMOS spectrometer 
 69ZN5c  at GANIL facility. Prompt gammas emitted by the recoil nuclei          
 69ZN6c  were detected using the EXOGAM array that consisted of four Ge clover  
 69ZN7c  detectors placed at 90|' and another at 135|' with respect to the      
 69ZN8c  beam direction. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, level lifetimes by       
 69ZN9c  RDDS technique using Cologne plunger device and EXOGAM array of Ge     
 69ZNac  detectors. Deduced levels, J, |p, level lifetimes, B(M1). Comparison   
 69ZNbc  with shell-model calculations                                          
