 69ZN c  2019Xi07: {+69}Zn was produced by bombarding UC{-x} target             
 69ZN2c  with 1.4 GeV proton beam at the CERN-ISOLDE facility.                  
 69ZN3c  Zn isotopes were selectively ionized by the RILIS laser ion source,    
 69ZN4c  accelerated to 30 keV, mass separated with the high-resolution mass    
 69ZN5c  separator, and injected into the COLLAPS setup. Measured hyperfine     
 69ZN6c  spectra and deduced changes in mean square charge radii relative to    
 69ZN8c  {+68}Zn. Systematic uncertainty are mainly from uncertainty on         
 69ZN9c  atomic and field-shift factors. Comparisons were done with             
 69ZNac  Monte Carlo Shell Model (MCSM) calculations.                           
 69ZN c  2017Wr01: {+69}Zn was produced by by bombarding UC{-x} target          
 69ZN2c  with 1.4 GeV proton beam at the CERN-ISOLDE facility.                  
 69ZN3c  Zn isotopes were selectively ionized by the RILIS laser ion source,    
 69ZN4c  accelerated to 30 keV, mass separated with the high-resolution mass    
 69ZN5c  separator, and injected into the COLLAPS setup. Measured hyperfine     
 69ZN6c  spectra using collinear laser spectroscopy using COLLAPS setup at      
 69ZN7c  ISOLDE-CERN. Deduced spins, |m, Q, isomer. Comparison with large-scale 
 69ZN8c  shell model calculations.                                              
 69ZN c  For the calibration of nuclear moments, |m=+0.875479 {I9} from         
 69ZN2c  literature and Q=+0.122 {I10} (2017Wr01) for the stable {+67}Zn nuclide
 69ZN3c  were used as references                                                
