 69GA    68ZN(P,G)                     1981PA12,1978RA06         26NDS    202601
 69GA  H TYP=FUL$AUT=C.D. NESARAJA$CIT=NDS 207, 1 (2026)$CUT=1-Apr-2023$        
 69GA c  1981Pa12: Protons with E=2-4 MeV were produced at the Tandem           
 69GA2c  Van de Graaff Accelerator Laboratory, NRC Demokritos and at the        
 69GA3c  CNRS-Strasbourg. The proton beams were incident on 3-4 mg/cm{+2}       
 69GA4c  thick self-supported {+68}Zn targets positioned at 45|' with           
 69GA5c  respect to the beam. Gammas were detected between 0|' and 150|'        
 69GA6c  using Ge(Li) detectors with FWHM=2.1-2.3 keV at 1.3 MeV.               
 69GA7c  Measured E|g, I|g, |g(|q), T{-1/2} from DSAM                           
 69GA c  1978Ra06: Proton beam E=3.2-3.8 MeV from the Universite Laval Van de   
 69GA2c  Graaff accelerator was used to bombard isotopically enriched           
 69GA3c  {+68}Zn target. Gammas were detected at lab angle 165|' using a Ge(Li) 
 69GA6c  detector with FWHM=3 keV at 1.3 MeV. Measured E|g, |G(|g), |s(E) and   
 69GA2c  M1 strengths                                                           
 69GA c  1971Ne06: Protons at E=2 MeV from the FTI AN UkrSSR electrostatic      
 69GA2c  accelerator impinging a self-supporting {+68}Zn target. Gammas were    
 69GA3c  were detected with a NaI(Tl) detector. Measured E|g, I|g,              
 69GA4c  |g|g coincidences                                                      
 69GA c  1973Ne07: Protons at E=2 MeV from the FTI AN UkrSSR electrostatic      
 69GA2c  accelerator impinged self-supporting 1.5-2.5 mg/cm{+2} {+68}Zn         
 69GA3c  targets. Gammas were detected with a NaI(Tl) detector.                 
 69GA4c  Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g coincidences, triple |g|g(|q). Statistical     
 69GAxc  theory analysis was performed on the experimental results.             
 69GA c  Other: 1983Ni04                                                        
 69GA c  Data for IAR and associated |g rays are from 1978Ra06                  
 69GA cG RI$Percentage branching from each level with no uncertainties          
 69GA2cG from 1981Pa12, unless indicated otherwise                              
 69GA cG RI(e)$From 1978Ra06                                                    
 69GA cG E(D)$Gammas were not listed in Table VII of 1981Pa12 but are given     
 69GA2cG in Fig.6 (1981Pa12) without uncertainties. The uncertainties for       
 69GA3cG these gammas were estimated by the evaluator from data in Table VII in 
 69GA4cG 1981Pa12                                                               
 69GA cG E(E)$Deduced from the level scheme of 1978Ra06                         
 69GA cG M$From |g(|q) (1981Pa12) and |D|p=no from level scheme,                
 69GA2cG unless indicated otherwise                                             
 69GA cG MR$From |g(|q) by 1981Pa12, unless indicated otherwise                 
 69GA cG M(F)$From |g(|q) in 1978Ra06                                           
