 69GA c  1974Ri08: {+3}He ions at 15 MeV produced from the E(n) Tandem Van de   
 69GA2c  Graaff accelerator in Heidelberg were incident on a self-supporting    
 69GA3c  |?100 |mg/cm{+2} {+68}Zn target. The deuterons were analysed with a    
 69GA4c  single-gap broad-range Browne-Buechner magnetic spectrograph           
 69GA5c  type recorded on photographic emulsion plates.                         
 69GA6c  Angular distributions were measured at laboratory angles from 5|'      
 69GA7c  to 35|' with FWHM=15-20 keV. Measured |s(|q), |q=5|'-35|'. DWBA        
 69GA8c  analysis was performed using the JULIE code.                           
