 69GA    U(N,X),U(P,X)                 2017FA09,2012PR11         26NDS    202601
 69GA  H TYP=FUL$AUT=C.D. NESARAJA$CIT=NDS 207, 1 (2026)$CUT=1-Apr-2023$        
 69GA c  2017Fa09: {+69}Ga was produced at the ISOLDE-CERN facility by          
 69GA2c  bombarding UCx target with neutrons. The neutrons were produced via    
 69GA2c  spallation process by 1.4 GeV proton beam incident on                  
 69GA3c  a solid tungsten neutron converter. The Ga isotopes were ionized using 
 69GA4c  the RILIS sources which was followed by mass separation using the      
 69GA5c  high-resolution mass separator. The properties were then studied       
 69GA6c  using the Collinear resonance ionization spectroscopy technique.       
 69GA7c  Deduced: spins, magnetic dipole and electric quadrupole moments,       
 69GA8c  and isotope shift. Comparison with large-scale shell-model calculations
 69GA9c  using JUN45 and GXPF1 interactions.                                    
 69GA c  2012Pr11: {+69}Ga was produced by impinging 1.4 GeV protons on the     
 69GA2c  UC{-x} target at ISOLDE-CERN facility. Fragments diffused out of target
 69GA3c  were first selectively ionized using the RILIS laser ion source and    
 69GA4c  then accelerated to 30 keV. The process was followed by mass separation
 69GA5c  and delivery to the ISODLE cooler-buncher, ISCOOL. Ions were released  
 69GA6c  the released in bunches toward the COLLPAS experimental beam line.     
 69GA7c  Isotope shifts were measured by collinear laser spectroscopy using     
 69GA8c  the COLLAPS setup. Deduced rms charge radius.                          
 69GA  L 0            3/2-                                                      
 69GA2 L MOMM1=+2.014 4 (2017Fa09)                                              
 69GA3 L MOME2=+0.167 24 (2017Fa09)                                             
