 69GE c  1997Be65: E|a=13-23 MeV from the tandem Van de                         
 69GE2c  Graff accelerator of the University of Cologne bombarded enriched      
 69GE3c  {+66}Zn targets that were backed by Bi-In-Cu layer. Gammas were        
 69GE5c  detected with Ge detectors (FWHM=2.1-2.4 keV at 1.33 MeV). |g|g        
 69GE6c  coincidence weremeasured with the OSIRIS cube spectrometer consisting  
 69GE7c  of six Compton-suppressed Ge detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, |g yield    
 69GE9c  functions, |g|g coin, |g(|q) and |g linear polarization                
 69GE c  1980KiZT: E|a|?45 MeV. Measured: T{-1/2} by delayed coincidence method 
 69GE c  1979Al08: E|a=11.8, 14 and 16.5 MeV beams bombarded thin {+66}Zn       
 69GE2c  foils. Gammas were detected with a Ge(Li) detector                     
 69GE3c  (FWHM=3.5 keV at 1330 keV). Measured: E|g, I|g, |g(|q) and             
 69GE2c  T{-1/2} by DSA.                                                        
 69GE c  1975Eb05: Alpha beams at E|a=13 and 19 MeV provided by the 7.5 MV      
 69GE2c  tandem accelerator of the University of Cologne bombarded              
 69GE3c  self-supporting enriched {+66}Zn targets. Gammas were detected with    
 69GE4c  Ge(Li) detectors. Measured E|g, |g|g coincidences, I|g, |g(|q),        
 69GE2c  |g yield functions and delayed |g|g coincidences.                      
 69GE c  1976Eb02: Alpha beams at E|a=12.5-16 MeV provided by the 7.5 MV tandem 
 69GE2c  accelerator of the University of Cologne bombarded self-supporting     
 69GE3c  enriched {+66}Zn targets. Gammas were detected with Ge(Li) detectors.  
 69GE4c  Measured E|g, I|g, linear polarization and T{-1/2} by DSA              
 69GE c  1974Fo12: E|a=10-14 MeV. E|g, |g|g coincidences, I|g, |g(|q), |g yield 
 69GE2c  functions and |g linear polarizations.                                 
