 69GE    69GA(P,NG)                    1978PA15,1973IS02         26NDS    202601
 69GE  H TYP=FUL$AUT=C.D. NESARAJA$CIT=NDS 207, 1 (2026)$CUT=1-Apr-2023$        
 69GE c  1978Pa15: Protons with E=3-5.6 MeV produced from the NRC Demokritos    
 69GE2c  Tl1/25 tandem Van de Graaff accelerator, Athens, Greece were incident  
 69GE3c  98% enriched Ga target. Gammas were measured with two Ge(Li)           
 69GE4c  detectors postioned at 90|' and 55|'. Measured E|g, I|g, |g(|q),       
 69GE2c  excitation functions and T{-1/2} by DSAM                               
 69GE c  1973Is02: E(p)=3.4-5.0 MeV were incident on enriched Ga{-2}O{-3}       
 69GE2c  targets. Gammas were detected with a Ge(Li)detector (FWHM=3.3 keV      
 69GE3c  at 1.33 MeV |g) at |q=90|'. Internal conversion electron were          
 69GE4c  detected with a in-beam sector field |b{+-} spectrometer.              
 69GE5c  Measured E|g, I|g, |a(exp) and excitation functions.                   
 69GE c  1970Ch05: |g(|q,H,t) and T{-1/2} for the 398 level by stroboscopic     
 69GE2c  observation of perturbed angular distributions                         
 69GE cG $Branching ratio from 1978Pa15                                         
 69GE cG E$Placed |g's are from 1978Pa15, unplaced |g's are from                
 69GExcG 1973Is02.                                                              
 69GE cG RI$Relative intensity, mostly from 1973Is02 measured at                
 69GE2cG E(p)=5.0 MeV, supplemented by branching ratio data from 1978Pa15.      
 69GE3cG These data are in reasonable agreement with those of 1973Is02.         
 69GE cG M$From |g(|q) and |D|p from level scheme.                              
 69GE2cG (1978Pa15), except as noted.                                           
 69GE cG M(A)$From |g(|q) and RUL                                               
 69GE cG MR$From |g(|q) (1978Pa15), except as noted.                            
 69GE2cG |a(exp) data of 1973Is02 are given in comments. The authors normalized 
 69GE3cG their data to |a{-k}(exp)=0.082 for the 174.8|g E2 transition in       
 69GE4cG {+71}Ge. Renormalization to |a{-k}(theory)=0.0808 {I12} from 2008Ki07  
 69GE5cG would not affect the conclusions                                       
 69GE cG RI(E)$1973Is02 report I|g=74 for the doubly placed 812 |g. From        
 69GE2cG branching in Adopted Gammas, one expects I|g=62 for placement from     
 69GE3cG the 812 level, leaving I|g=12 for placement from the 1210 level.       
 69GE4cG From Adopted Gammas, the 397.9 and 1210 |g's have a branching of |?    
 69GE5cG 10 % that of the 812 |g                                                
 69GE cG RI(F)$The 778.62 |g and 1192.7 |g are unplaced by 1973Is02. The        
 69GE2cG authors' ratio of I|g(1192|g)/I|g(779|g)=1.35 is inconsistent          
 69GE3cG with 0.32 {5} from 1978Pa15 and 0.52 {I10} from (|a,n|g)               
 69GE cL E$From least-squares fit to E|g data by the evaluator.                 
