 69GE  H TYP=FUL$AUT=C.D. NESARAJA$CIT=NDS 207, 1 (2026)$CUT=1-Apr-2023$        
 69GE c  {+60}Ni({+12}C,2pn|g):                                                 
 69GE c  1997Be65: {+12}C ions with E=48, 56, 60 MeV from the tandem Van de     
 69GE2c  Graff accelerator of the University of Cologne bombarded enriched      
 69GE3c  {+60}Ni targets that were backed by Bi-In-Cu layer. Targets were       
 69GE4c  self-supporting for the lifetime measurements. Gammas were detected    
 69GE5c  with Ge detectors (FWHM=2.1-2.4 keV at 1.33 MeV). Measured E|g, I|g,   
 69GE6c  |g yield functions, |g|g coin. and T{-1/2} by recoil-distance          
 69GE7c  Doppler shift (RDDS) method.                                           
 69GE c                                                                         
 69GE c  {+55}Mn({+16}O,np|g):                                                  
 69GE c  1979Zo02: {+16}O ions with E=40-51 MeV from the tandem Van de          
 69GE2c  Graff accelerator of the University of Cologne bombarded natural       
 69GE3c  {+55}Mn targets. |g|g coin. were detected with two Ge(Li) detectors,   
 69GE4c  placed 90|' and 27|' to the beam axis. Measured E|g, |g|g coin, I|g,   
 69GE5c  |g(|q), |g-ray linear polarization and T{-1/2} by recoil distance.     
 69GE c  1979Pa13: {+16}O beam from the Strasbourg MP tandem accelerator at     
 69GE2c  various energies stated below bombarded pure {+55}Mn targets. Gammas   
 69GE3c  were detected with various Ge(Li) dtectors (FWHM=2-2.5 keV). Below is  
 69GE4c  listed the measurements performed at the different beam energies.      
 69GE c  E=47.5 MeV; E|g, |g|g coincidences, I|g and |g(|q)                     
 69GE c  E=42.5 MeV; |g(|q).                                                    
 69GE c  E=37.5-50 MeV; |g-ray yield functions.                                 
 69GE c                                                                         
 69GE c  {+64}Zn({+7}Li,np|g):                                                  
 69GE c  1982Pa03: {+7}Li ions at E=15-18 MeV from the T11/25 tandem Van de     
 69GE2c  Graaff accelerator in Greece bombarded enriched {+64}Zn targets.       
 69GE3c  Gammas were detected with Ge(Li) detectors. Measured |g(|q),           
 69GE4c  |g ray yield functions at angles 0|', 90|' and 110|' with respect      
 69GE5c  to the beam and T{-1/2} by DSAM.                                       
