 69GE c  2021Ha10: Photon-induced measurements were performed with              
 69GE2c  bremsstrahlung photons from the Madison Accelerator Laboratory         
 69GE3c  (MAL) at James Madison University. Enriched {+70}Ge target was         
 69GE4c  irradiated with these bremssthrahlung photons with endpoint            
 69GE5c  energy of 15 MeV. Gammas were detected with a HPGe detector,           
 69GE6c  enclosed into an ultra low-background lead shield. Measured            
 69GE7c  E|g, |g(t) and T{-1/2}.                                                
 69GE  L 0           5/2-              38.82 H   8                              
 69GE cL J$from the Adopted levels                                              
 69GE cL T$Deduced from decay curves for the 574.11|g, 871.98|g and             
 69GE2cL 1106.77|g. Activity was counted for over 6 half-lives.                 
 69GE3cL 38.82 h {I7} (stat) {I4} (syst) reported by 2021Ha10 is                
 69GE4cL the weighted average of 38.68 h {I13} (stat) {I2} (syst),              
 69GE4cL 38.76 h {I23} (stat) {I3} (syst), and                                  
 69GE5cL 38.90 h {I9} (stat) {I1} (syst).                                       
 69GE5cL 38.82 h {I8} is the combined uncertainties in quadrature               

