 69GE c  Also contains ({+3}He,t) data                                          
 69GE c  {+69}Ga({+3}He,t):                                                     
 69GE c  1988Ch38: {+3}He beam at E=29.8 MeV from the Princeton AVF cyclotron   
 69GE2c  bombarded a natural {+69}Ga target. Tritons were detected in singles at
 69GE3c  |q{-lab}=0|' at the focal plane of a QDDD magnetic spectrometer.       
 69GE4c  Decay products in coincidence with tritons were detected with a Si     
 69GE5c  surface barrier detector. Measured |s(E(t)), particle spectrum from    
 69GE6c  the decay of the IAS in {+68}Ge at 7.00 {I5} MeV.                      
 69GE7c  Deduced |a-decay branching from the IAS.                               
 69GE c                                                                         
 69GE c  {+70}Ge({+3}He,|a):                                                    
 69GE c  1967Fo05: {+3}He beam at E=18 MeV from the University of Pennsylvania  
 69GE2c  Tandem Accelerator was used to bombard {+70}Ge targets in a scattering 
 69GE3c  chamber. Alpha particles were detected with eight Si surface barrier   
 69GE4c  detectors. Measured |s(|q) at |q|?0|'-120|'. Performed DWBA            
 69GE5c  calculations (JULIE code) to analyze the data and to extract           
 69GE6c  spectroscopic factors.                                                 
 69GE cL L$From DWBA analysis of |s(|q).                                        
 69GE cL J$Assumed to extract spectroscopic factors                             
 69GE CL S$LABEL=C2S                                                            
 69GE cL S$Uncertainties in absolute values estimated by authors (1967Fo05)     
 69GE2cL to be about 20%.                                                       
