 69AS  H TYP=FUL$AUT=C.D. NESARAJA$CIT=NDS 207, 1 (2026)$CUT=1-Apr-2023$        
 69AS dL E$Least-squares fitting is done by GLSC (version 17-Jan-2025)          
 69AS c  1988De28: {+69}Se was produced from {+40}Ca({+32}S,2pn).               
 69AS2c  Gammas were detected by Ge(Li)counters with 20% efficiency. Emitted    
 69AS3c  protons were detected with the Si(Au) surface barrier counter with     
 69AS4c  FWHM typically 18 keV for composite |a source of {+239}Pu,{+241}Am,    
 69AS5c  {+244}Cm. Measured |e delayed p, |g, and |b{++}, E|g, I|g, |g|g and    
 69AS6c  p|g coincidences using the recoil transport helium jet technique.      
 69AS7c  Authors assume that all the observed transitions are                   
 69AS8c  Gamow-Teller and conclude that the sum over all of them over an        
 69AS9c  energy range of about 6.5 MeV is equal to 0.23 or 7.7% of the sum rule 
 69ASac  limit of 3.                                                            
 69AS c  1977Ma24: {+69}Se was produced from {+40}Ca({+32}S,2pn) at the         
 69AS2c  Chalk River tandem. Gammas were detected with a Ge(Li) detector.       
 69AS3c  For detection of gammas in coincidence and X-rays, Ge X-ray detectors  
 69AS4c  were used. Measured |e delayed p, |g, and |b{++} spectra, E|g, I|g,    
 69AS2c  and |g|g, |b{++}|g, p|g, pX-ray and |gX-ray coincidences and |a(K)exp. 
 69AS c  Other: 1973Pr12.                                                       
 69AS cE TI(A)$ From intensity balances. No direct measurements of the g.s.     
 69AS2cE branch have been made. From a measurement of the annihilation          
 69AS3cE radiation, 1977Ma24 deduce a g.s. branch of 19% {I12}, and 1988De28    
 69AS4cE using their revised decay scheme and the annihilation measurement of   
 69AS5cE 1977Ma24 deduce a g.s. branch of <23% . Both authors                   
 69AS6cE assume J|p({+69}Se g.s.)=3/2-. See 1989Ar13 for a discussion of this   
 69AS7cE feeding. With J|p({+69}Se g.s.) established as 1/2-, any decay to the  
 69AS8cE 5/2- g.s. will be negligible (an expected log {Ift} > 12.8 gives       
 69AS9cE I(|e+|b{++})<2 x10{+-6} %). The evaluator has revised the decay        
 69ASacE scheme so that the g.s. feeding is zero. The I|g normalization now is  
 69ASbcE 0.85 {I4} compared with 0.78 {I10} for a g.s. branch of 22% {I10}, and 
 69ASccE the log {Ift} values for the excited levels are slightly smaller. No   
 69ASdcE changes in J|p assignments for the {+69}As levels are necessary        
 69AS cE TI(B)$From the delayed proton spectrum (1988De28)                      
 69AS cG E,RI$Weighted average data from 1988De28 and 1977Ma24, unless indicated
 69AS2cG otherwise                                                              
 69AS cG E(D),RI(D)$ From 1977Ma24. Not reported by 1988De28                    
 69AS cG E(F),RI(F)$ From 1988De28. Not reported by 1977Ma24                    
 69AS cG M,MR$From Adopted Gammas; which were deduced from |a(K)exp in this     
 69AS2cG dataset.                                                               
 69AS cG CC(X)$Calculated from |a(K)exp and |a(K)/|a (BrIcc). |a(K)exp have     
 69AS2cG been recalculated from the values in 1977Ma24 by 2000Bh05 using the    
 69AS3cG fluorescent yield from 1972Bb16.                                       
 69AS cL E$From a least-squares fit to the E|g data by the evaluator. Levels at 
 69AS2cL 4649 and above were deduced by 1988De28 from measurements of proton    
 69AS3cL energy emitted from these levels and the assumption that the proton    
 69AS4cL feeding is essentially 98.6 % (1977Ma24) to the ground state of        
 69AS5cL {+68}Ge. A proton separation energy of 3391 {I30} keV was adopted by   
 69AS6cL 1988De28 for {+69}As and a recoil correction was applied. The levels   
 69AS7cL have been updated by the evaluator using the current value             
 69AS8cL S(p)=3420 {I30} in 2021Wa16. These levels have not been included in    
 69AS9cL the Adopted Levels as none of them are likely to correspond to the     
 69ASacL gamma decaying levels.                                                 
