 69AS    40CA(32S,3PG)                 2004ST23                  26NDS    202601
 69AS  H TYP=FUL$AUT=C.D. NESARAJA$CIT=NDS 207, 1 (2026)$CUT=1-Apr-2023$        
 69AS c  2019Ma78: {+32}S beam at E=95 MeV was produced from the Tandem XTU     
 69AS2c  accelerator of the INFN Laboratori Nazionali di Legnaro, Legnaro,      
 69AS3c  Italy. The beam struck a 0.8 mg/cm{+2} {+40}Ca foil which              
 69AS4c  had carbon layer on both sides to avoid fast oxidation                 
 69AS5c  Gammas were detected with a 4|p-GASP array that consisted of           
 69AS6c  37 Compton-suppressed HPGe detectors symmetrically arranged in seven   
 69AS7c  rings located at 35|', 60|', 72|', 90|', 108|', 120|', and 145|'       
 69AS8c  with respect to the beam axis. The evaporation residues were detected  
 69AS9c  by the recoil filter detector. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g. Deduced T{-1/2}
 69ASac  using the Doppler-shift attenuation method (DSAM).                     
 69AS c  2004St23: {+32}S beams at E=105 MeV and E=95 MeV produced from         
 69AS2c  the VIVITRON accelerator at the IReS Strasbourg impinged a self        
 69AS3c  supporting {+40}Ca target and Au backed {+40}Ca target, repectively.   
 69AS4c  Gammas were detected with the EUROBALL array consisting of 15          
 69AS5c  Cluster and 26 Clover composite Ge detectors each surrounded by a      
 69AS6c  bismuth germanate shield providing Compton suppression. Charged        
 69AS7c  particles were detected using the 4|p device EUCLIDES, composed of     
 69AS8c  40 |DE-E Si telescopes with the five forward elements electrically     
 69AS9c  segmented into four parts. The evaporated neutrons were detected with  
 69ASac  the Neutron Wall, consisting of 50 liquid scintillators covering the   
 69ASbc  1|p section of EUROBALL. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g, |g|g|g, |g(|q)(DCO). 
 69AScc  No evidence was found for superdeformation in {+69}As in the very high 
 69ASdc  counting statistics experiment. High spin bands were interpreted using 
 69ASec  cranked Nilsson-Strutinsky calculations.                               
 69AS c  2000Br38: {+32}S beam at E=105 MeV produced from the Holifield         
 69AS2c  Radioactive Ion Beam Facility at Oak Ridge National Laboratory was     
 69AS3c  incident on natural Ca target. Gammas were detected using and array    
 69AS4c  of five 'clover' detectors and six suppressed Ge detectors.            
 69AS5c  Measured E|g and |g|g                                                  
 69AS c  1997MiZY: {+32}S beam at E=140 MeV was incident on natural Ca target   
 69AS2c  with Au backing. In-beam |g|g coincidence measurements was performed   
 69AS3c  with the JAERI mini crystal ball with 11 anti-compton Ge spectrometer  
 69AS4c  in combination with 21 Si charged particles detectors. Measured data   
 69AS5c  are not given by authors.                                              
 69AS c  1974No08: {+32}S beam at E=100 MeV produced from the Munich MP Tandem  
 69AS2c  accelerator was incident on a Ca target. Gammas were detected with     
 69AS3c  Ge(Li) detectors. Measured E|g, I|g and |g|g coincidences              
