 69SE    40CA(32S,2PNG)                2004ST09,2001JE10         26NDS    202601
 69SE  H TYP=FUL$AUT=C.D. NESARAJA$CIT=NDS 207, 1 (2026)$CUT=1-Apr-2023$        
 69SE dL E$Least-squares fitting is done by GLSC (version 17-Jan-2025)          
 69SE c  2004St09: E=105 MeV, 95 MeV {+32}S beam at the VIVITRON accelerator at 
 69SE2c  Strasbourg were incident on self supporting and gold backed Ca targets,
 69SE3c  respectively. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g, |g|g(|q)(DCO), |g(|q), n|g|g    
 69SE3c  and n|g|g|g. The EUROBALL array consisting of 15 Cluster and 26 Clover 
 69SE4c  composite Ge-detectors surrounded by a BGO shield providing escape     
 69SE5c  suppression were used for |g-ray detection.                            
 69SE6c  Charged particles were detected using the 4|p device EUCLIDES          
 69SE7c  consisting of 40 |DE-E Si telescopes. Evaporated neutrons were         
 69SE8c  detected with the Neutron Wall consisting of 50 liquid scintillators   
 69SE9c  covering 1|p section of EUROBALL                                       
 69SE c  2001Je10: E({+32}S)=100 MeV beam from the ATLAS accelerator at Argonne 
 69SE2c  National Laboratory bombarded a thick {+40}Ca target. Gammas were      
 69SE3c  detected by the Gammasphere array consisting of 80 HPGe detectors.     
 69SE4c  Neutrons and charged particles were detected with 30 neutron detectors 
 69SE5c  and the Microball array consisting of 95 CsI detectors, respectively.  
 69SE6c  Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g, |g|g(|q)(DCO)                                 
 69SE c  1998Sk04: Includes {+32}S({+40}Ca,2pn|g) reaction. E({+40}Ca)=125 MeV  
 69SE2c  beam from the accelerator facilty of the Max-Planck Institut in        
 69SE3c  Heidelberg bombarded a {+32}S cooled target. Gammas were detected with 
 69SE3c  the Euroball Cluster detectors. Measured E|g, I|g and T{-1/2}.         
 69SE c  1995Po01: E({+32}S)=96 MeV ions produced by the University of          
 69SE2c  Pennsylvania tandem bombarded a 100 |mg/cm{+2} enriched {+40}Ca        
 69SE3c  target. Charged particles and gammas were detected with the            
 69SE4c  Penn 4|p array which is a segmented array of charged particle          
 69SE5c  detectors covering approximately 70% of 4|p along with three           
 69SE6c  germanium detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, |g(|q), charged particle       
 69SE2c  (CP)-|g coin, |g|g delayed coin, T{-1/2} and |a(exp)                   
 69SE c  1989Ar13: E({+32}S)=76-105 MeV beams from the Van de Graaff accelerator
 69SE2c  at the University of Pennsylvania bombarded 300-500 |mg cm{+2} {+40}Ca 
 69SE3c  targets. Charged particles (CP) and gammas were detected with a        
 69SE4c  4|p phoswich array, Ge and NaI(Tl) detectors. Neutrons were detected   
 69SE5c  liquid scintillator. Measured CP-|g coin as a function of beam         
 69SE2c  energy, CP-n-|g coin, CP-|g|g coin, n-|g|g coin, n|g(|q), |b-|g coin   
 69SExc  and T{-1/2}.                                                           
 69SE c  1988Wi02: E({+32}S)=100 MeV beam from ; E|g, I|g, |g and n|g           
 69SE2c  excitation functions, |g|g coincidence the Cologne FN Tandem           
 69SE3c  accelerator bombarded a {+40}Ca target. Gammas and neutrons were       
 69SE4c  detected with the OSIRIS Anticompton spectrometer in combination with  
 69SE5c  a neutron multiplicity filter. Measured prompt and delayed conversion  
 69SE3c  electron spectra, n-gated |g(|q), T{-1/2}. Uncertainties in E|g, I|g   
 69SE4c  and other experimental details have not been given. Isomeric state     
 69SE5c  observed and has been associated with oblate deformed configuration.   
 69SE c  1988Ra06: E({+32}S)=80-110 MeV beam from the Centre de Recherches      
 69SE2c  Nucleaires tandem Van de Graaff facility bombarded a {+40}Ca target.   
 69SE3c  Low energy gammas were measured a two Ge(Li) detectors positioned      
 69SE4c  at 135|' and 90|' to the beam axis. Neutrons were detected with a large
 69SE5c  scintillation counter. Measured E|g, I|g, |g-ray excitation            
 69SE2c  functions in coincidence with neutrons, |g|gn coincidences and T{-1/2}.
 69SE c  Other: 1997Og02                                                        
