 69SE    9BE(70SE,69SEG)               2015NI01                  26NDS    202601
 69SE  H TYP=FUL$AUT=C.D. NESARAJA$CIT=NDS 207, 1 (2026)$CUT=1-Apr-2023$        
 69SE c  No significant changes from XUNDL compiled dataset by                  
 69SE2c  J. Chen (NSCL, MSU), January 26, 2015, except for an unplaced          
 69SE3c  gamma by 2015Ni01 that has been included by the evaluator in this      
 69SE4c  dataset.                                                               
 69SE c  2015Ni01: E=175 MeV/nucleon {+78}Kr primary beam was produced from the 
 69SE2c  Coupled Cyclotron Facility at the National Superconducting Cyclotron   
 69SE3c  Laboratory (NSCL) and fragmented on a 399 mg/cm{+2} {+9}Be production  
 69SE4c  target. The secondary beam of {+70}Se was selected using the A1900     
 69SE5c  fragment separator which then bombarded the 96 mg/cm{+2} {+9}Be        
 69SE8c  secondary target housed at the target position of the S800             
 69SE9c  spectrograph. Reaction products were identified on an event-by-event   
 69SEac  basis from energy-loss and time-of-flight information using an         
 69SEbc  ionization chamber and plastic scintillators, respectively. |g rays    
 69SEcc  were measured by the SeGA array of segmented high-purity germanium     
 69SEdc  detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, |g-ray line shapes. Deduced levels,      
 69SEec  lifetimes using the |g-ray line-shape method. Experimental results     
 69SEfc  were compared with shell model calculations.                           
 69SE cL E$From least-squares fit to E|g data by the evaluator. No uncertainties
 69SE2cL are available for the E|g data. The least-squares fit is performed with
 69SE3cL the assumption that the uncertainties are the same for all the E|g     
 69SE4cL data. The evaluator notes that the least-squares fit gave a reduced    
 69SE5cL |h{+2}|?0 which could mean that the gammas provided by the authors     
 69SE6cL may be modified from level energy difference and are not the actual    
 69SE7cL measured values                                                        
 69SE cL T$Lifetimes were extracted by comparing the experimental |g-ray        
 69SE2cL lineshapes spectra after Doppler-broadening correction to GEANT        
 69SE3cL simulations (2015Ni01). The effect of lifetimes on the                 
 69SE4cL Doppler-reconstructed lineshapes of |g-ray spectra at relativistic     
 69SE5cL recoil energies is to cause |g emissions at different locations along  
 69SE6cL the beam axis in the target, which results in different                
 69SE7cL Doppler-broadening corrections that distort the lineshapes.            
 69SE PN                                                                     5  
 69SE  G 524       3                                                            
 69SE cG E$Too weak for coincidence measurement, and hence could not be placed  
 69SE2cG in the level scheme by 2015Ni01. Shell model calculations using GXPFIA 
 69SE3cG interaction predict J=(1/2,3/2,5/2) (2015Ni01)                         
