 69BR    ADOPTED LEVELS                                          26NDS    202601
 69BR  H TYP=FUL$AUT=C.D. NESARAJA$CIT=NDS 207, 1 (2026)$CUT=1-Apr-2023$        
 69BR c  Dataset prepared by F. Kondev (ANL) and C.D. Nesaraja (ORNL)           
 69BR  Q -14120    SY 15540  SY -640   40 -1750  90    2021WA16                 
 69BR cQ $|DQ(|b{+-})=300, |DS(n)=260 (syst,2021Wa16)                           
 69BR cQ $S(2n)=29870 {I300} (syst), S(2p)=4250 {I40}, Q(|ep)=5350 {I40}        
 69BR2cQ (2021Wa16)                                                             
 69BR c  2011Ro18: {+69}Br was produced in the fragmentation of a E=140 MeV/u   
 69BR2c  {+78}Kr beam incident on a {+9}Be target at NSCL, MSU. The reaction    
 69BR3c  products were selected by the S800 spectrograph and identified by their
 69BR4c  energy loss and time of flight. Emitted protons were detected by the   
 69BR5c  High Resolution Array (HIRA) with sixteen |DE-E telescopes,            
 69BR6c  each configured with a double-sided silicon strip detector and backed  
 69BR7c  by four CsI(Tl) crystals. Measured: Ep, implant-p(t) coin.             
 69BR c  1996Pf01: Searched for {+69}Br in the fragmentation of {+78}Kr         
 69BR2c  projectile with 75 MeV/u on a {+58}Ni target. Estimated T{-1/2} from   
 69BR3c  the absence of {+69}Br.                                                
 69BR c  1995Bl06: Found no evidence for {+69}Br in the fragmentation of        
 69BR2c  {+78}Kr beam at 73 MeV/u on a Ni target. Deduced that {+69}Br is proton
 69BR3c  unbound by at least 450 keV to yield a T{-1/2} less than about 100 ns. 
 69BR c  1995He39: Attempt to measure the |b{++} decay half-life of {+69}Br in  
 69BR2c  the fragmentation of {+78}Kr at 70 MeV/u on a natural Ni target was not
 69BR3c  successful because of low count rate.                                  
 69BR c  1995MoZV: searched for {+69}Br in the fragmentation of a 75 MeV/u      
 69BR2c  {+78}Kr beam incident on a {+58}Ni target. No events that could be     
 69BR3c  attributed to {+69}Br were observed.                                   
 69BR c  1991Mo10: identified {+69}Br activity in the fragmentation of {+78}Kr  
 69BR2c  beam at 65 MeV/u on an enriched {+58}Ni target. However, the authors   
 69BR3c  state that it is difficult to conclude from such a small number of     
 69BR4c  events whether {+69}Br has been in fact identified or whether the      
 69BR5c  events are due to background processes.                                
 69BR c  1990Ro15: searched for the g.s. p decays of {+69}Br using the          
 69BR2c  {+40}Ca({+32}S,p2n) reaction with E({+32}S)=200 MeV. No p groups that  
 69BR3c  could be assigned to {+69}Br were observed. If the production cross    
 69BR4c  section of {+69}Br is of the order of 150 microbarns, then {+69}Br     
 69BR5c  must have p half-life shorter than 300 |ms or longer than 30 ms.       
 69BR c  1989Ho19: searched for p radioactivity of {+69}Br using the            
 69BR2c  {+40}Ca({+32}S,p2n) reaction. Found no p radioactivity in the energy   
 69BR3c  range 250-600 keV and a T{-1/2} range of 10 |ms -100 ms and a          
 69BR4c  production cross section lower limit of 1 microbarn.                   
 69BR c  Others: 1999Ja02, 1997Or04, 1989HoZG, 1989HoZQ, 1978BaYE, 1977JaZT     
 69BR  XA69KR EC DECAY (27.9 MS)                                                
 69BR  L 0.0         (5/2-)            24 NS     LT                             
 69BR2 L %P=100                                                                 
 69BRX L XREF=A                                                                 
 69BR3 L ISPIN=1/2                                                              
 69BR cL J$From 2014De41, based on shell-model predictions and direct population
 69BR2cL from {+69}Kr |b{++}+|e decay [J|p=(5/2-)]. log {Ift}=5.54 in {+69}Kr   
 69BR3cL |b{++}+|e decay [J|p=(5/2-)] would be consistent with J|p=3/2- or 5/2-,
 69BR4cL but would exclude a possible J|p=1/2- assignment. Note, that J|p=5/2-  
 69BR5cL for the ground state of the neighboring {+71}Br (Z=35) nucleus and     
 69BR6cL J|p=1/2- for the ground state of the {+69}Se (N=35) mirror nucleus.    
 69BR2cL The assignment is tentative.                                           
 69BR cL T$From 1996Pf01. Others: <100 ns (1995Bl06), <30 ns (1995MoZV)         
 69BR cL CONF$Probable configuration=|pf{-5/2}{++1}                             
